fec-fun-epitaph = [italic]Epitaph: { $text }[/italic]
fec-fun-epitaph-1 = Checked if it was loaded. It was.
fec-fun-epitaph-2 = Last words: "It's just a runner".
fec-fun-epitaph-3 = Lived without armor, died the same way.
fec-fun-epitaph-4 = Posthumous medal for bravery in front of a resin wall.
fec-fun-epitaph-5 = Wanted to ask the queen for directions to medbay.
fec-fun-epitaph-6 = The flamethrower did not fire where expected.
fec-fun-epitaph-7 = One step into the storm was the last.
fec-fun-epitaph-8 = Bravely covered the retreat. Nobody was retreating.
fec-fun-epitaph-9 = The last MRE remains unopened.
fec-fun-epitaph-10 = The commander said "forward". This marine went first.
fec-fun-epitaph-11 = Joined the USCM to travel. The trip is over.
fec-fun-epitaph-12 = The weather report gave a warning. Nobody read it.
fec-fun-epitaph-13 = Here lies a marine who took the helmet off "for a second".
fec-fun-epitaph-14 = The medic was busy. Always.
fec-fun-epitaph-15 = Fell bravely. The bravery was unnecessary.
fec-fun-epitaph-16 = The pizza never arrived.
fec-fun-epitaph-17 = Mom always said: "stay out of the vents".
fec-fun-epitaph-18 = The dropship was two steps away. There were more steps.
fec-fun-epitaph-19 = ARES logged it in the report. No details.
fec-fun-epitaph-20 = They found the grenade. Not the pin.

fec-fun-ares-tip = ARES tip of the day. { $text }
fec-fun-ares-tip-1 = Armor works better when worn.
fec-fun-ares-tip-2 = The flamethrower is not a cabin heater.
fec-fun-ares-tip-3 = Medbay reminds you: a bandage does not fix a missing arm.
fec-fun-ares-tip-4 = The helmet protects the head. The head is required for duty.
fec-fun-ares-tip-5 = Check your magazine before deployment. An empty magazine is still a magazine, just worse.
fec-fun-ares-tip-6 = Do not feed the xenomorphs. They feed themselves.
fec-fun-ares-tip-7 = The weather report exists. Read it.
fec-fun-ares-tip-8 = A squad that sticks together comes back together.
fec-fun-ares-tip-9 = Ventilation is not a tactical route.
fec-fun-ares-tip-10 = Pizza aboard is not part of rations. The source of the pizza is under investigation.
fec-fun-ares-tip-11 = Grenades fly farther if you pull the pin first.
fec-fun-ares-tip-12 = Orders are to be followed. Grumbling is allowed, quietly.
fec-fun-ares-tip-13 = If you hear hissing in the dark, it is not the air conditioning.
fec-fun-ares-tip-14 = The number of marines aboard should match the number returning aboard.
fec-fun-ares-tip-15 = ARES wishes you a productive shift and minimal casualties.

fec-prank-say = Say a line
fec-prank-honk = Honk
fec-prank-balloon = Balloon
fec-prank-spin = Spin
fec-prank-button = Prank
fec-prank-go = Prank
fec-prank-hint = Harmless pranks for events. Each one goes into the admin log.
fec-prank-unknown = Unknown prank "{ $prank }". Available: say, honk, balloon, spin
fec-prank-done = { $player } pranked: { $prank }
fec-prank-honk-popup = A bike horn suddenly appears!
fec-prank-balloon-popup = Someone gave you a balloon!
fec-prank-spin-popup = Your head is spinning!
fec-prank-line-1 = I see a xeno! Oh, no, that's my shadow.
fec-prank-line-2 = Has anyone seen my MRE?
fec-prank-line-3 = Sarge, can I stay on the ship today?
fec-prank-line-4 = I love the smell of napalm in the morning.
fec-prank-line-5 = I know exactly where to go. Almost.
fec-prank-line-6 = I'll cover you. From a distance.
fec-prank-line-7 = Who ordered pizza?
fec-prank-line-8 = This resin looks comfy.
fec-prank-line-9 = I think ARES is watching me.
fec-prank-line-10 = Medic! Oh, never mind. Medic!
fec-prank-line-11 = I could really use some leave on Earth.
fec-prank-line-12 = Great weather for a drop today. Probably.
fec-prank-line-13 = This helmet is too tight.
fec-prank-line-14 = Does anyone know how this thing works?
fec-prank-line-15 = Hooah! For the USCM! Which way are we running?

cmd-fecprank-desc = Harmless prank on a player.
cmd-fecprank-help = Usage: fecprank <username> <say|honk|balloon|spin>
